# Blind PRE: local formation background and ordered factorial intensity

Date: 2026-09-24. This is an independent reconstruction before release of the root's local-background candidate. It concerns the supplied compensated common rotor process. All scientific imports remain conditional and unaudited. No author calculation, active checker packet, campaign checkpoint, magnetic-lag packet or microscopic packet was read. No delegation, publication edit, audit decision or new physical premise is included.

**Result.** On finite simple cubic even-period tori with periods at least six, the full supplied generator admits the following comparison for a fixed bounded local observable:

\[
\left|\operatorname{Tr}O_X\bigl(e^{t\mathcal L_\kappa}\rho-
 e^{t\mathcal L_0}\rho\bigr)\right|
\le \|O_X\|\min\{2,C_X\kappa t(1+\delta t)^3\}.
\tag{1}
\]

Here \(\mathcal L_0\rho=-i[KD+\delta H_4^C,\rho]\), and \(\mathcal L_\kappa\) adds **all** channels of the original resolved or coherent formation instrument. The constant depends on the fixed support and cubic degree, but not on total volume, \(K\), the electric field, the initial normal physical density, or \(\kappa,\delta,t\). It is deliberately loose. In fact (1) follows from an operator-norm estimate, with explicit constants below. The norm means the norm of the chosen bounded local representative in the ambient tensor algebra; its restriction to the physical Gauss subspace is understood.

The relevant zero-lag ordered **factorial** intensity, allowing arbitrary other events, is exactly \(\kappa^2\operatorname{Tr}O_{ij}\rho_\kappa(t)\), with the full local effect \(O_{ij}=(B_jB_i)^*(B_jB_i)\). Thus (1) controls its formation-background error without a global survival factor. The scalar-plus-plaquette identity applies only to its initial-sector restriction. The estimate does not prove that a fixed nonzero formation rate preserves an arbitrarily small weak-field signal at a fixed positive time; it does not provide a uniform finite-lag or microscopic derivative limit.

